  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up Protection Assistance to IDPs and IDP returnees in newly accessible woredas of Tigray, Amhara and Afar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This UNHCR project aims to provide critical life-saving protection services and assistance to internally displaced people, returnees, and others affected persons in newly accessible woredas of Tigray, Amhara, and Afar.  The project alleviates protection risks and threats through IDP return monitoring, Protection Case Management Supporting Persons with Specific Needs, and provision of Protection &#x2013; Housing Land and Property Services.  In total, UNHCR is reaching 35,415 people , including 7,750 women, 775 men, and 27,000 children including 700 Persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
